========================================================
1. OBJECTIVE
========================================================

Build a Python-based static SQL analyzer that scans SQL files
containing approximately 400–500+ lines and identifies
hardcoded values embedded in SQL logic.

The purpose is to identify values that may need to be:
- parameterized
- moved to configuration
- moved to reference/master tables
- converted to ADF parameters
- reviewed during SQL/ADF migration

The analyzer must NOT simply extract every string.

It must understand the surrounding SQL context.

Example:

WHERE BSET.KSCHL IN
(
    'XR1',
    'XR2',
    'XR3',
    'XR4',
    'XRS',
    'XR6',
    'XP1E',
    'XP2E',
    'XP3E',
    'XP4E'
)

AND NVL(BSET.SLT_DELETE, '') <> 'X'

Expected hardcoded values:

XR1
XR2
XR3
XR4
XRS
XR6
XP1E
XP2E
XP3E
XP4E
X

The following are NOT hardcoded values:

BSET.KSCHL
BSET.SLT_DELETE

because they are column references.

